-- title:
--   Pullback of the dual of an invertible ideal sheaf
-- statement:
--   Let $X$ and $X'$ be schemes (in a fixed universe), let $f \colon X' \to X$ be a morphism of schemes, and let $I$ be an ideal sheaf datum on $X$. Assume $I$ is invertible in the sense of the predicate `IsInvertible`: for every point $x$ of $X$ there are an affine open $U \subseteq X$ and a section $s \in \Gamma(X, U)$ with $x$ in the basic open set of $s$, together with a non-zero-divisor $g$ in the ring of the affine basic open set of $s$ such that the ideal of $I$ on that affine basic open set is the principal ideal generated by $g$. Assume moreover that the inverse-image ideal sheaf $I.\mathrm{comap}\ f$ on $X'$ is invertible in the same sense. The conclusion is that the type of isomorphisms in the category $X'.\mathrm{Modules}$ between $f^{*}(I^{\vee})$ and $(I.\mathrm{comap}\ f)^{\vee}$ is non-empty; here, for an ideal sheaf datum $J$, $J.\mathrm{invModule}$ is the internal-hom dual $(\mathrm{ihom}\ J.\mathrm{module}).\mathrm{obj}\ \mathbb{1}$ of the module $J.\mathrm{module}$, the kernel of the map from the structure sheaf to the pushforward of the structure sheaf of the closed subscheme cut out by $J$. So the assertion is the existence of an isomorphism, with no canonical choice or naturality claimed.
--
--   This is the statement that $f^{*}\mathcal O_X(Z) \cong \mathcal O_{X'}(f^{-1}Z)$ for an invertible ideal sheaf whose inverse image is again invertible, the dual half of the compatibility of $\mathcal O(\pm Z)$ with base change. It is used for relative effective Cartier divisors on curves, where pulling a divisor back along a base change replaces the ideal by its comap, and feeds into the line-bundle and relative Picard constructions.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_AlgebraicGeometry_Scheme_IdealSheafData_IsInvertible_nonempty_pullback_invModule_iso.lean

